  "dom_id": "step-q3928",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "${(27{u}^{6}{v}^{-3/5})}^{-2/3}=$",
  "worked_solution": "We apply the power of product rule and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(27{u}^{6}{v}^{-3/5})}^{-2/3} & = \\\\ {({3}^{3}{u}^{6}{v}^{-3/5})}^{-2/3} & = \\\\ {({3}^{3})}^{-2/3}\\cdot {({u}^{6})}^{-2/3}\\cdot {({v}^{-3/5})}^{-2/3} & = \\\\ {3}^{3\\cdot (-2/3)}\\cdot {u}^{6\\cdot (-2/3)}\\cdot {v}^{(-3/5)\\cdot (-2/3)} & = \\\\ {3}^{-6/3}\\cdot {u}^{-12/3}\\cdot {v}^{6/15} & = \\\\ {3}^{-2}\\cdot {u}^{-4}\\cdot {v}^{2/5} & = \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2/5}}{{3}^{2}{u}^{4}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2/5}}{9{u}^{4}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
